/* Aspect readings for the IC (home and roots) and the Descendant (partnership). */
window.AstroDeep = window.AstroDeep || {};
window.AstroDeep.aspectsRich = window.AstroDeep.aspectsRich || {};
Object.assign(window.AstroDeep.aspectsRich, {
  "sun|ic": {
    theme: "Your sense of self is rooted in home and family. Who you are grows from where you come from, and much of your light shines in private before it shines anywhere else.",
    fusion: "Your identity sits at the very root of your chart, so home is where you feel most yourself. You draw strength from family, heritage and a private base that belongs to you, and you tend to pour real pride into the place you live and the people in it. A parent, often the father, shaped your sense of who you are more deeply than you realise. The difficulty is that you can hide your brightness indoors, keeping your best self for the few who see you at home. Recognition from the wider world matters less to you than feeling solid underneath. Over time your life builds towards a home and a lineage you are proud of, and your later years often bring your warmest confidence.",
    flow: "Confidence and belonging feed each other in you. You carry a steady sense of where you come from, and it gives you an ease that others notice without being able to name. Family tends to support who you are becoming, or you have found a way to make peace with your roots that leaves you stronger. You create a home with a clear personality, a place that reflects you. Comfort can leave you resting on a comfortable base rather than stretching further. Your foundation is a genuine gift, and it lets you grow outward with a calm certainty that you can always come back to yourself.",
    tension: "Your need to shine and your need for a private base keep pulling against each other. Part of you wants to be seen and to make your mark, and part of you wants to retreat into home and be nobody in particular. Family expectations around who you ought to become press on your sense of self, and you can feel you have to leave your roots to be yourself, or give yourself up to keep the peace at home. Old tension with a parent still flares when you make big choices. Working through this gives you an identity that is truly your own, built from your roots rather than in spite of them."
  },
  "moon|ic": {
    theme: "Your emotional life and your roots are one and the same. You need a real home to feel safe, and family memories live close to the surface of every feeling.",
    fusion: "Home is not a place for you so much as a feeling you cannot live without. You need a nest, somewhere familiar and private, and when you have it you are calm in a way nothing else provides. Your mother or the main carer of your childhood left a deep imprint on your moods, and you carry family patterns in your body as much as your mind. You nurture instinctively, and people feel looked after in the space you create. The shadow is clinging: to the past, to old hurts, to people and places long after they have stopped feeding you. As life goes on, your belonging grows from the inside, and the home you build becomes a genuine refuge for others too.",
    flow: "Feeling safe comes fairly naturally to you, and it gives you an emotional steadiness others lean on. You sense the mood of a household almost instantly, and you know how to soften it. Early bonds with family, or at least with one caring figure, gave you a reliable sense that you are held. You are good at making any place feel lived in and warm. The risk is staying too cosy, choosing the familiar because it soothes you rather than because it suits you. At its best, your gift for belonging becomes a quiet anchor, and the people around you settle simply because you are there.",
    tension: "Your emotional needs and your home life rarely line up neatly. You long for a secure base, yet the demands of the wider world, or your own restlessness, keep pulling you away from it. Moods from childhood can surge up without warning, and old family dynamics replay when you are tired or under pressure. You can feel torn between caring for your people and caring for your own path, with guilt either way. When the balance tips, you feel unmoored and scattered. This friction teaches you to carry home within you, and in time you become someone who can offer others the security you had to find for yourself."
  },
  "mercury|ic": {
    theme: "Your mind is shaped by the conversations and ideas you grew up with. Home is where you think best, and your family's way of speaking still lives in yours.",
    fusion: "Your thinking is rooted in home. The ideas, stories and turns of phrase you absorbed in your family formed the lens you still see through, and you often process the world by talking it over with those closest to you. Your private life tends to be full of information, talk and plans, and you think most clearly on familiar ground. You are curious about your background and good at piecing together where things came from. The difficulty is a restless mind at home, turning family matters over long after they are settled. With time, your understanding of your roots becomes a real gift, and you can explain your people, and yourself, with rare clarity.",
    flow: "Words come easily between you and the people you live with. You grew up with, or have since built, a household where things can be talked about, and that openness steadies you. You can name what is happening in a family long before anyone else can, and relatives often rely on you to explain, mediate or keep everyone informed. Your memory for your own history is sharp, and you learn a lot from it. Your quickness can lead you to chatter over feelings that need silence rather than analysis. When your mind and your roots work together, you become the one who makes sense of where everyone has come from.",
    tension: "Your mind and your private life keep interrupting each other. Busy thoughts about work, plans and outside demands follow you into the home, and household matters break your concentration when you need to focus. You can feel that your family never quite understood how you think, or that your ideas were talked over when you were young. Conversations with relatives turn tense quickly, with old misunderstandings resurfacing. Restlessness can keep you changing addresses or feeling mentally unsettled wherever you live. Over time this friction sharpens your voice, and you learn to speak about your roots honestly, with a clarity that helps others make sense of their own."
  },
  "venus|ic": {
    theme: "Love and beauty sit at the root of your life. You need a home that feels harmonious, and affection within the family is what makes you feel whole.",
    fusion: "You carry a deep need for a home that is beautiful, peaceful and full of affection. Harmony in your private life matters more to you than almost anything, and you put real care into making your surroundings pleasing and welcoming. Warm memories of family, or a longing for the warmth you missed, shape what you value. People feel at ease in the space you create, and you often become the one who smooths things over at home. The shadow is avoiding conflict at any cost, keeping the peace when something needs to be said. As life unfolds, your home becomes a source of genuine pleasure, and your later years tend to be gentle and rich in love.",
    flow: "Affection and belonging flow easily for you. You have a natural gift for making a home comfortable and lovely, and family relationships tend to carry a sweetness that others notice. You value your roots and find something to appreciate in where you come from, even the parts that were hard. Your private life often becomes the centre of your happiness, and people you love are drawn back to you again and again. All that sweetness can tip into indulgence or a reluctance to leave comfort behind. At its best, your talent for harmony turns any house into a real home and gives you a deep, lasting sense of contentment.",
    tension: "What you love and where you belong do not always sit comfortably together. Your desire for pleasure, beauty or a certain kind of relationship can clash with the expectations of family, and you can feel that loving freely means stepping away from your roots. Tension at home affects you more than you show, and you tend to smooth it over rather than face it. Spending or indulgence can become a way of soothing unease in your private life. Choosing between your own heart and your family's approval is a recurring theme. The friction eventually teaches you what you truly value, and the home you build reflects that rather than anyone else's taste."
  },
  "mars|ic": {
    theme: "Your drive is rooted in home and family. Energy, fight and protectiveness live at the base of your life, and your private world is where your fire burns hottest.",
    fusion: "There is a fierce energy at the base of your life. You protect your home and your people instinctively, and anyone who threatens them meets a side of you others rarely see. Early family life often carried conflict, competition or a strong need to fend for yourself, and that left you tough and independent. You pour effort into building and improving your base, and restlessness sets in when your private life stagnates. The difficulty is temper at home, where frustration from elsewhere can spill onto the people closest to you. Channelled well, this fire builds a strong foundation, and your later years carry a vigour that surprises people.",
    flow: "Energy and belonging support each other in you. You have the drive to create the home you want and the stamina to keep it going, and you tend to take charge of family matters when action is needed. Your roots gave you courage, or at least a sense that you can stand your ground. You are quick to defend your people and good at getting a household moving. Your speed can make you impatient with those who move more slowly than you do. At its best, your energy gives your private life momentum and warmth, and the people you live with feel safe because they know you will act.",
    tension: "Your drive and your home life keep clashing. Ambition and the urge to act pull you outward, while family needs and private responsibilities pull you back, and the friction shows up as irritation, impatience or open argument. Old battles from childhood can reignite quickly, especially with a parent or sibling. You can feel you have to fight for space of your own, or that home is where you burn off frustration you could not express elsewhere. This restlessness can keep you from settling anywhere for long. Learning to direct the fire rather than suppress it gives you the strength to build a foundation that genuinely belongs to you."
  },
  "jupiter|ic": {
    theme: "Your roots carry a sense of plenty. Home is where you grow, and faith, generosity or a wide family story gives you a broad and hopeful base.",
    fusion: "Your foundations feel generous and expansive. You grew up with, or have gone on to create, a sense that home is a place of abundance, learning and open doors. Family often brings you luck, support or a strong set of beliefs, and your private life tends to be larger than most, with room for many people and ideas. You feel happiest with space to roam, and a cramped life at home leaves you restless. The shadow is excess: taking on too much, overextending or expecting home to supply endless comfort. Over time your base grows richer, and later life often brings real contentment, security and a sense of having been blessed.",
    flow: "Growth and belonging work together for you. Your roots give you optimism, and you tend to feel that the world is basically a friendly place because home taught you so. Family traditions, faith or a love of learning passed down through relatives give you something solid to build on. You are generous with the people you live with and quick to open your door. Being so blessed can lead you to take good fortune for granted or avoid the harder work of maintaining what you have. At its best, your home becomes a place where people grow, and your later years tend to be expansive and warm.",
    tension: "Your hunger to grow and your need for a home base pull in different directions. Big plans, study or ambition draw you out into the world, and family life can feel small by comparison, or your wider hopes crowd out time with the people who need you. Your family often held beliefs you had to outgrow, and that disagreement still lingers. There is a tendency to promise more at home than you can deliver. The friction shows you that growth needs a foundation as much as a horizon, and when you honour both, your life gains a breadth and generosity others find inspiring."
  },
  "saturn|ic": {
    theme: "Your roots carry weight and responsibility. You build your foundations slowly and seriously, and security at home is something you earn rather than assume.",
    fusion: "Home asks a lot of you. Early family life often felt strict, cool or burdened by responsibility, and you learned young to rely on yourself and take things seriously. There can be a lingering sense that you do not quite belong, or that security has to be worked for. You approach your private life with care and caution, building your base one solid piece at a time. The difficulty is carrying old heaviness, duty or loneliness long after the need for it has passed. Yet what you build lasts. Later life is often where you come into your own, with a home and a sense of belonging that are genuinely yours.",
    flow: "Stability comes to you through patience. You have a practical, steady approach to home and family, and people trust you to keep things running when life gets hard. Your roots gave you discipline, respect for tradition or a clear sense of duty that still serves you. You tend to build security gradually and wisely, and your foundations rarely crumble. The shadow is a reserve at home that keeps warmth at arm's length, or a habit of seeing family life mainly as obligation. At your best you provide structure that others lean on, and your sense of belonging deepens year by year.",
    tension: "Your responsibilities and your private life are often at odds. Work, ambition or duty to the wider world can crowd out time at home, and family obligations can feel like weights that slow your progress. You grew up feeling you had to earn your place, and that pressure still shapes how you judge yourself. Home can feel more like a job than a refuge. Old fears about security make you cautious about putting down roots. Facing this friction steadily brings real strength, and over time you build a foundation that no outside pressure can shake, one grounded in your own authority."
  },
  "uranus|ic": {
    theme: "Your roots are unusual and your need for freedom starts at home. Belonging, for you, means a base that lets you be entirely yourself.",
    fusion: "Your foundations are anything but conventional. Family life was often unpredictable, unusual or marked by sudden changes, and you learned early that stability can vanish overnight. As a result, you need a home that gives you freedom and room to be different, and you resist any arrangement that feels confining. You often feel like the odd one out in your family, yet you bring fresh air into it. The difficulty is restlessness at the root: moving, rearranging or pulling away just as things settle. In time you build a way of belonging that is truly original, and later life often brings a liberation you did not expect.",
    flow: "Independence and belonging sit comfortably together in you. You can make a home in unusual ways and feel at ease with a family life that does not follow the usual script. Your roots gave you permission to think differently, or you made peace with being the one who broke the mould. You adapt quickly when your private life changes and often welcome the shake up. Your independence can leave you a little detached, loyal to your freedom more than to the people you live with. At its best, you create a base that is lively, open and free, a place where others feel allowed to be themselves.",
    tension: "Your need for freedom and your need for roots keep colliding. Sudden changes in direction, restless ambitions or a drive to be different pull you away from home just as family life asks for steadiness. Early disruption left you wary of depending on anyone, and you can keep one foot out of the door without meaning to. Family members find you hard to pin down, and you can find them hard to breathe around. Unexpected upheavals in your private life tend to arrive at turning points. This friction eventually shows you a way of belonging built on choice rather than obligation, and that freedom lets you stay."
  },
  "neptune|ic": {
    theme: "Your roots are soft, dreamy and hard to define. Home is a feeling you long for, and your family story carries mystery, idealism or sacrifice.",
    fusion: "Something elusive lives at the root of your life. Your early home felt magical, unclear or quietly unstable, and parts of your family story remain hazy to you. You long for a sanctuary, a place of peace and beauty where you can retreat from the harshness of the world. You pick up the unspoken moods of a household and often absorb them as your own. The shadow is idealising home or family, then feeling let down, or losing yourself in caring for others. Over time your sense of belonging becomes spiritual rather than literal, and your later years often carry a deep, quiet peace.",
    flow: "Your private life carries a gentle, intuitive quality. You create homes that feel calm and restorative, and people often say they relax the moment they are near you. You sense what family members need without being told and respond with compassion. Your roots gave you imagination, faith or a strong feeling for what cannot be seen. Softness can make you drift, avoiding practical matters at home or seeing people as you wish they were. At its best, your home becomes a genuine refuge, and your feeling of belonging extends to something larger than any one place or family.",
    tension: "Your dreams and your home life often blur into confusion. Ideals about what you should become, or longings that pull you towards something beyond ordinary life, can leave your private base neglected or unclear. Family life often involved secrets, absence or someone who needed rescuing, and you still find it hard to set boundaries with the people you love. You can feel you never had a solid footing, or that home keeps dissolving just as you settle. Escapism is the temptation. This friction ultimately teaches you to build a foundation that is both real and meaningful, where compassion does not cost you yourself."
  },
  "pluto|ic": {
    theme: "Your roots run deep and carry power. Home and family are where you have been most transformed, and belonging, for you, is intense and all or nothing.",
    fusion: "The foundations of your life carry great intensity. Early family life held hidden power struggles, loss, secrets or a force that shaped everyone in its path, and you took in more than you could name at the time. You feel things at home deeply and need a private life that allows total honesty. Control over your own space matters enormously to you. The difficulty is carrying family patterns you never chose and repeating them without seeing it. Yet your roots are also a source of immense strength. Over time you transform what you inherited, and later life often brings a profound sense of renewal and self possession.",
    flow: "Depth and belonging work together in you. You have an instinct for what lies beneath family life and can face difficult truths at home without flinching. You tend to renew your private life when it grows stale, clearing out what no longer serves you, and you draw real power from your roots. Relatives often turn to you in a crisis because you stay steady when others fall apart. The shadow is a need for control in your home that can feel heavy to others. At its best, you become the one who breaks old cycles, leaving your family line stronger than you found it.",
    tension: "Your drive for power and your private life keep testing each other. Ambitions and the need for control out in the world collide with intense family dynamics, and crises at home often arrive at the same moments that your outer life demands the most. Old struggles over power with a parent still echo in the way you handle authority. Home can feel like a battleground, or like something you must fight to keep. Letting go is hard for you. Through this friction you undergo real transformation, and the strength you build reshapes both your roots and your direction, until what once controlled you becomes a source of power."
  },
  "chiron|ic": {
    theme: "Your deepest wound lies in home and belonging. Where you felt unsafe or out of place becomes the very place you learn to heal, and to help others heal.",
    fusion: "There is a tender place at the root of your life. Some part of you felt you did not belong in your family, or that home was not the refuge it should have been, and that ache runs quietly beneath many of your choices. You can feel like an outsider even among people who love you. The difficulty is protecting the wound so carefully that you struggle to settle anywhere. Yet this is also where your gift lies. You understand displacement and longing from the inside, and others feel it. Over time you build a home that heals, and you become a place of belonging for people who never had one.",
    flow: "Your old hurts around home have become a source of understanding. You can talk about family pain without being swallowed by it, and people often confide in you about their own roots. You know how to make someone feel welcome, perhaps because you remember what it was like not to. Your private life has a gentle, healing quality, and you tend to repair what is broken in family bonds. The risk is caring for everyone else's wounds while leaving your own untended. At its best, your sensitivity to belonging makes you a quiet healer, and your home becomes a place of real acceptance.",
    tension: "The wound around belonging keeps rubbing against the rest of your life. Pressure in the outer world, or your own striving, can reopen old feelings of not being at home anywhere, and family matters touch raw nerves quickly. You can feel you have to prove your worth before you can rest, or that success will finally make you feel you belong. Retreating from home to escape the ache is a familiar pattern. This friction is painful, yet it is also the path to healing: through it you learn to give yourself the sense of home you once lacked, and your hard won understanding becomes a gift you pass on."
  },
  "northNode|ic": {
    theme: "Your growth points towards home, family and inner life. Building roots and nurturing your private world is the direction your life keeps asking you to take.",
    fusion: "Your path of growth runs straight through home and family. You are drawn, sometimes reluctantly, towards building roots, caring for your people and developing an inner life that does not depend on outside recognition. Part of you is used to striving, achieving and being judged by results, and you can feel uneasy slowing down. The difficulty is resisting the pull of the private world because it feels less important than public goals. Yet every step towards belonging feels right in a way success alone never does. Over time, home becomes the source of your fulfilment, and your emotional foundations become the ground of your purpose.",
    flow: "Growth comes to you through your private life. Nurturing a home, deepening family bonds and exploring your roots all move you forward, and opportunities for this arrive with surprising ease. You have a natural gift for balancing outer duties with inner needs. Family or ancestry often opens doors for you or offers insight into who you are becoming. Because it comes so naturally, you can undervalue this path, treating home as a side matter. At its best, your commitment to your foundations brings you steady, lasting fulfilment, and you grow into someone deeply at peace with where you come from.",
    tension: "Your direction of growth and your private life are not easily reconciled. Your path asks you to stretch towards something new, and home, family or the comfort of the familiar can hold you back from it. You feel torn between what you came to become and what your people expect, and old family roles fit you less with every year. Returning to the safety of home when growth feels frightening is a strong temptation. Yet your roots are not the enemy. Through this friction you learn to carry your foundations with you, and moving forward grows easier once home stops being a hiding place and becomes a launching point."
  },
  "lilith|ic": {
    theme: "Your wild, unapologetic side is rooted in family life. Something raw or rejected lives at home, and reclaiming it is part of finding where you truly belong.",
    fusion: "A fierce, untamed part of you lives at the root of your life. Your early home held something suppressed, shamed or taboo, a rebellious streak in the family line or a part of you that was not welcome. You feel strongly about owning your private space on your own terms and resist anyone who tries to dictate how you live. You often feel an outsider to family norms, especially around the roles you were expected to play. The difficulty is carrying shame or rage from the past that surfaces in your most intimate settings. Over time you reclaim your roots, and your home becomes a place where your whole self is allowed.",
    flow: "You have made a kind of peace with the untamed side of your roots. You live privately by your own rules and feel little need to explain yourself to family. Parts of your heritage that others might hide, you tend to accept or even celebrate. You create a home where people can drop their masks, and your honesty about the messier sides of family life frees others to be honest too. Your freedom from it can make you dismissive of tradition altogether. At its best, you turn your private world into a place of real authenticity, where no part of anyone needs exiling.",
    tension: "Your untamed side and your home life keep clashing. The part of you that refuses to conform pushes against family expectations, and home can feel like a place where you are asked to be smaller than you are. Old anger about how you were treated, or about roles you were pushed into, rises when you least expect it. You can swing between rebelling against your roots and cutting yourself off from them entirely. Standing out in the world sometimes feels like a betrayal of your people. This friction eventually frees you, and you learn to belong without shrinking and to rebel without losing your ground."
  },
  "fortune|ic": {
    theme: "Your luck and ease are found at home. Joy comes most readily through family, roots and a private life that truly nourishes you.",
    fusion: "Your good fortune lives at the base of your life. You feel happiest, luckiest and most at ease when your home is settled and your private life is in order. Family, property or heritage often bring you benefits, and simple things such as belonging and familiarity give you a deep contentment. You thrive when you invest in your foundations. The difficulty is overlooking this source of joy while chasing happiness elsewhere, or depending on home for all your wellbeing. As life goes on, your base becomes richer, and later years often bring a steady, satisfying sense of having arrived exactly where you belong.",
    flow: "Contentment flows easily between you and your roots. You tend to find happiness through family, a comfortable home and a sense of continuity with the past. Good things come to you when you nurture your private life, and people close to you often bring you luck. You have a knack for creating a base that supports your wellbeing without much strain. Contentment can turn complacent, relying on familiar comforts rather than seeking new sources of joy. At its best, your home life becomes a well you can always draw from, and that inner abundance spills into everything else you do.",
    tension: "Your happiness and your home life do not always match up. What brings you joy can pull you away from family or your private base, and what home offers can feel short of what truly fulfils you. You tend to chase contentment in outer achievement while neglecting the foundation that would sustain it, or to cling to home comforts that no longer satisfy. Family expectations about what a good life looks like clash with your own sense of it. Through this friction you discover what genuinely nourishes you, and your joy deepens and steadies once it rests on a foundation you have chosen for yourself."
  },
  "vertex|ic": {
    theme: "Fated encounters shape your home and family life. People and events that seem to arrive by destiny change where and how you belong.",
    fusion: "Destiny touches the root of your life. Encounters that feel meant to be often change your home, family or sense of belonging, sometimes suddenly and in ways you could never have planned. Some people arrive and become family, and some turns of events uproot you and set you down somewhere new. You feel a strong pull towards the past, towards ancestry and the patterns handed down to you. The difficulty is feeling your private life is shaped by forces beyond your control. Yet each fated turn brings you closer to where you truly belong, and your later years often reveal the thread running through it all.",
    flow: "Fated meetings tend to bring you closer to home. People who appear at key moments often become part of your inner circle or help you settle and put down roots. You sense when someone or something is meant to become part of your private life, and you accept these turning points with grace. Family connections can arrive in unexpected ways. Trusting fate can make you passive, waiting for destiny rather than building. At its best, these encounters weave together a sense of belonging that feels guided, as if your home and your people were always meant to find you.",
    tension: "Destined encounters and your home life pull against each other. People or events that feel fated unsettle your private world, demanding changes to family arrangements or pulling you away from your roots. Your sense of belonging is continually tested by forces you did not choose. Meetings that shape your direction in the world sometimes come at a cost to home. Resisting these turning points only makes them more disruptive. Through the friction you come to understand that fate is reshaping your foundations for a reason, and the home you eventually build carries the imprint of every meeting that shook it."
  }
});

Object.assign(window.AstroDeep.aspectsRich, {
  "sun|dsc": {
    theme: "Your sense of self comes alive through partnership. You come to know who you are in the mirror of the people closest to you.",
    fusion: "You shine most fully when you are paired with someone. A committed relationship is where your confidence, purpose and vitality come into focus, and on your own you can feel strangely half formed. You are drawn to partners with strong personalities, people who carry a brightness you admire and have not yet fully claimed in yourself. Others experience you as generous and loyal in a relationship, someone who invests completely once the commitment is made. The shadow is handing your identity over, letting a partner's goals and opinions stand in for your own, or choosing people who outshine you. Over time you learn that the light you see in them is also yours, and your partnerships become meetings of equals.",
    flow: "Relationships come easily to you, and they tend to strengthen rather than drain you. You know how to be fully yourself with another person without losing your centre, and partners feel both seen and respected in your company. You attract people who admire you openly, and you return that warmth with real loyalty. Close business partnerships suit you as much as love does, because you bring clarity and good faith to any shared venture. The ease can make you lean on one to one bonds for validation more than you realise, measuring your worth by how a partner responds to you. At your best you show how two strong people can stand side by side, each brighter for the other.",
    tension: "Your need to be yourself and your need for a partner pull in different directions. You want a relationship to support your purpose, yet you bristle when a partner has plans of their own, or you give way so completely that you lose track of what you wanted. Struggles over who leads are familiar territory, and you can attract people whose pride rivals yours. Sometimes you insist on independence while privately longing for someone to share your life with. This friction teaches you the difference between a partner who competes with you and one who completes the picture. Once your sense of self no longer depends on winning or yielding, partnership becomes a place where you both grow."
  },
  "moon|dsc": {
    theme: "You need emotional closeness in partnership to feel safe. The people you commit to become your home, and you read their moods as closely as your own.",
    fusion: "Partnership is where you feel most at home, and being single rarely feels natural for long. You look for someone who offers emotional safety, warmth and a sense of family, and you give the same in return with great tenderness. You sense a partner's feelings almost before they do, and you adjust to them instinctively. People often come to you for care, so you can attract those who need looking after. The difficulty is that your mood rises and falls with the state of your closest bond, and need can be mistaken for love. As you learn to hold your own feelings steadily, your relationships become a true shelter rather than a lifeline.",
    flow: "Emotional openness comes easily to you in close relationships. You make partners feel understood, and you tend to attract people who are nurturing, loyal and emotionally available. Your instinct for what someone needs lets you soothe tension before it hardens, so your bonds tend to feel settled and kind. Family and partnership blend naturally in your life, and you want a relationship that feels like a shared home. Comfort can become the goal in itself, keeping you in a familiar bond after it has stopped nourishing you, simply because leaving feels unsafe. At its best your gift for care creates relationships where both people feel secure enough to grow.",
    tension: "Your emotional needs and the demands of a partnership rarely line up neatly. Part of you craves closeness and reassurance, while another part protects its privacy and resents being depended on. You can swing between clinging and withdrawing, and a partner's moods unsettle you more than you let them see. Old family patterns tend to replay in your relationships, especially around care, dependency and who looks after whom. Partners can arrive who are either too needy or too distant for comfort. This friction slowly teaches you to name your feelings rather than expect them to be guessed. When you do, closeness stops feeling like a risk and starts to feel like rest."
  },
  "mercury|dsc": {
    theme: "Conversation is the heart of your relationships. You are drawn to minds that keep you thinking, and partnership is where your ideas find their echo.",
    fusion: "You fall for minds before anything else. A partner has to be someone you can talk to for hours, trade ideas with and learn from, and a relationship without lively conversation fades quickly for you. You tend to attract clever, articulate or restless people, often young in spirit and quick with words. Negotiation comes naturally, so you are good at working out agreements in love and business alike. The shadow is living in your head in relationships, analysing feelings rather than feeling them, or letting a partner's opinions shape your own too readily. Over time your partnerships become places where honest words build real understanding, and where you feel truly heard.",
    flow: "Communication flows easily between you and the people you are closest to. You know how to explain yourself without wounding, how to listen without losing your own view, and how to find the words that settle a disagreement. Partners appreciate your curiosity and the way you keep a relationship mentally alive, full of shared jokes, plans and discoveries. You often form strong working partnerships built on shared ideas, contracts or projects. The ease can tempt you to talk around difficult feelings instead of through them, keeping things pleasant but slightly on the surface. When your words carry your heart as well as your mind, your bonds gain real depth and trust.",
    tension: "What you think and what your partner hears often come apart. You can feel misunderstood in close relationships, or find yourself arguing about details when the real issue lies deeper. Part of you wants intellectual freedom and room to change your mind, while partnership asks for consistency and follow through. You may attract people who talk over you, or become the one who dominates the conversation. Nervous energy around commitment can show up as overthinking every sign and signal. This friction sharpens your ability to say what you mean and to hear what lies beneath another person's words. Eventually you become a skilled mediator, in love and beyond."
  },
  "venus|dsc": {
    theme: "Love and harmony shape how you partner. You attract affection easily and seek relationships that feel beautiful, fair and mutually devoted.",
    fusion: "Partnership is one of the great pleasures of your life, and love tends to find you with little effort. People find you gracious, warm and easy to be close to, and you bring kindness and a sense of fairness to every committed bond. You are drawn to partners who are attractive, refined or artistic, and you value harmony highly. Close business relationships also tend to go well, because people enjoy working with you. The shadow is idealising a partner, avoiding necessary conflict or measuring your worth by whether you are loved. As you grow, your relationships become an expression of your own values rather than a search for approval, and they grow richer for it.",
    flow: "Affection moves easily between you and the people you commit to. You know how to make a partner feel cherished, and you have a gift for smoothing over friction with tact and generosity. You tend to attract kind, sociable partners, and relationships often bring you comfort, beauty and even material ease. People enjoy cooperating with you, which makes shared ventures pleasant as well as productive. The very ease can make you reluctant to face the harder conversations a lasting bond needs, so small resentments go unspoken for longer than they should. When grace and honesty work together, your partnerships become quietly remarkable.",
    tension: "What you desire and what partnership demands are often at odds. You want love to feel easy and beautiful, yet relationships keep asking you to compromise, confront and give up some of your own comfort. You may attract partners whose values differ sharply from yours, or feel torn between attraction and good sense. Jealousy, people pleasing or keeping score can creep in when you feel unappreciated. Sometimes you hold back affection to protect yourself, then feel puzzled when closeness stays out of reach. This friction teaches you what you truly value in another person. Once you know it, you choose love with far more wisdom and receive it more fully."
  },
  "mars|dsc": {
    theme: "Partnership is where your drive, desire and temper come alive. You are drawn to strong, spirited people, and your relationships carry real heat.",
    fusion: "Passion and friction arrive together in your closest bonds. You are drawn to assertive, energetic or competitive partners, and you often meet your own fire through them before you fully own it yourself. Relationships feel vivid, physical and alive, and you have little patience for a lukewarm connection. You fight for the people you love and bring courage to any shared venture. The difficulty is conflict: arguments flare quickly, and you can attract partners who push, provoke or dominate. As you claim your own anger and desire directly, you stop needing a partner to carry them, and your relationships become energising rather than exhausting.",
    flow: "Desire and action work together in your relationships. You pursue the people you want with confidence, and you bring energy, initiative and a healthy appetite to partnership. Partners find you exciting and dependable in a crisis, because you act rather than wait. You work well alongside others toward shared goals, and a good disagreement tends to clear the air rather than damage trust. The ease can make you impatient with slower or gentler partners, pushing the pace of a relationship faster than the other person is ready for. When your fire is balanced by patience, you become a partner who makes things happen for both of you.",
    tension: "Your independence and your partnerships keep colliding. You want to act on your own terms, yet close relationships ask you to consider another person's pace and wishes, and that can feel like a leash. Arguments, rivalry and struggles for control are common themes, and you may attract partners who are combative or who bring out your own temper. Sometimes the anger turns inward and you comply while seething quietly. Desire can be strong and complicated, pulling you toward people who are exciting rather than kind. This friction teaches you to fight fairly and to assert yourself without attacking. Out of it comes a partnership style that is honest, direct and alive."
  },
  "jupiter|dsc": {
    theme: "Partnership brings you growth, luck and a wider world. You are drawn to generous, expansive people, and your relationships tend to enlarge your life.",
    fusion: "Relationships are one of the great sources of good fortune in your life. You attract partners who are generous, optimistic, worldly or wise, and through them your horizons widen considerably. Marriage and close business partnerships often bring opportunity, support or even prosperity. You are a warm, encouraging partner who believes in the people you love. The shadow is expecting too much, overlooking a partner's flaws in your enthusiasm, or seeking a relationship that promises more than it can deliver. You can also crave so much freedom that commitment feels confining. As your faith in others matures into sound judgement, partnership becomes a genuine blessing.",
    flow: "Good will flows through your relationships. You tend to attract partners who support your growth, and you bring generosity, humour and a spirit of adventure to every close bond. People feel lifted by your optimism, and contracts or agreements you enter often work out well. You are tolerant of differences, which helps relationships with people from other backgrounds or beliefs flourish. The ease can make you complacent, assuming things will sort themselves out without effort, or promising more than you have time to give. When your openness is joined by commitment, your partnerships become a source of meaning as well as happiness.",
    tension: "Your hunger for freedom and your commitment to a partner can pull hard against each other. You want a relationship that broadens your life, yet you may feel boxed in once it becomes routine. Overpromising is a familiar pattern, as is expecting a partner to supply your happiness, meaning or sense of purpose. Differences in beliefs, values or lifestyle tend to surface in close bonds, and you can become preachy or restless when you feel unsatisfied. Sometimes the grass looks greener in another relationship altogether. This friction teaches you that growth can happen inside commitment as well as beyond it. With that understood, your relationships become generous and genuinely expansive."
  },
  "saturn|dsc": {
    theme: "You take partnership seriously. Commitment, loyalty and responsibility shape your relationships, and love tends to grow stronger the longer it lasts.",
    fusion: "Commitment weighs heavily with you, and you rarely enter a relationship lightly. You are drawn to partners who are older, established, reserved or responsible, people who offer stability and structure. Relationships can arrive later in life or after a long period of caution, and the ones you choose are built to last. You are loyal, dependable and willing to do the work a lasting bond requires. The difficulty is fear: of rejection, of dependence or of choosing wrongly, which can keep you guarded or in a relationship that feels more like duty than love. With time and maturity, your partnerships become deeply trustworthy and quietly rich.",
    flow: "Steadiness is the gift you bring to partnership. You understand that lasting relationships are built through patience, reliability and shared effort, and partners feel secure knowing you mean what you promise. You tend to attract mature, grounded people, and business partnerships benefit from your sense of responsibility. Relationships improve with age for you, gaining depth and trust as the years pass. The caution can make you slow to open up or reluctant to show vulnerability, so partners sometimes wait a long time to see your softer side. When your seriousness is warmed by tenderness, your partnerships become a solid foundation for a good life.",
    tension: "Your need for control and the vulnerability that partnership demands sit uneasily together. You want security in a relationship, yet commitment can feel heavy, restricting or frightening, as if closeness brings a burden with it. You may attract partners who are critical, cold or controlling, or become the one who holds back affection and keeps score. Delays, obstacles or a lingering sense of loneliness within a relationship can feel familiar. Old fears of rejection shape how much you let people in. This friction is demanding, but it builds real emotional maturity. Slowly you learn that commitment can hold you rather than confine you, and your bonds become deeply reliable."
  },
  "uranus|dsc": {
    theme: "You need freedom and surprise in partnership. You are drawn to unusual, independent people, and your relationships rarely follow a conventional script.",
    fusion: "Conventional relationships rarely suit you. You are drawn to partners who are original, independent, unpredictable or unlike anyone you have known, and attraction often strikes suddenly. Your bonds need room to breathe, with plenty of space for each person's individuality. Relationships can begin or end abruptly, and you may find yourself in arrangements others do not understand. The difficulty is instability: you crave closeness and freedom at the same time, attracting people who cannot commit or keeping one foot out the door yourself. As you accept your need for a different kind of partnership, you create bonds that are honest, stimulating and truly your own.",
    flow: "Freedom and closeness sit comfortably together in your relationships. You attract lively, original partners, and you give the people you love plenty of room to be themselves. Friendship tends to lie at the heart of your bonds, and you are open to arrangements that suit the two of you rather than tradition. Partnerships often bring fresh ideas and unexpected turns that keep your life interesting and moving forward. The ease can make you detached, stepping back into your own head when emotions run high and a partner wants you close. When your independence is joined by steady presence, your relationships feel both exciting and secure.",
    tension: "Your need for independence and your wish for partnership keep clashing. Just as a relationship begins to feel settled, restlessness stirs and you want out, or a partner suddenly pulls away without warning. Unexpected breakups, sudden attractions and on again off again patterns can mark your history. Part of you fears being trapped, while another part longs for someone who truly accepts your strangeness. You may attract people who are exciting but unreliable. This friction pushes you to design relationships that honour freedom without abandoning commitment. Once you stop running from closeness, you find partnerships that are alive, honest and free."
  },
  "neptune|dsc": {
    theme: "You long for a soulmate. Partnership carries a dreamy, spiritual quality for you, and you see the ideal in the people you love.",
    fusion: "Partnership carries a romantic, almost spiritual longing for you. You look for a soulmate, someone with whom you can merge completely, and you are drawn to sensitive, artistic, compassionate or elusive people. You love with great tenderness and sacrifice readily for a partner. The difficulty is seeing clearly: you tend to idealise the people you love, overlook warning signs, or attract partners who need rescuing or who are not fully available. Disillusionment can follow when the dream meets reality. As you learn to love people as they are rather than as you imagine them, your capacity for compassionate, soulful partnership becomes a genuine gift.",
    flow: "Tenderness and imagination flow easily into your relationships. You sense a partner's feelings intuitively, and you bring compassion, romance and a gentle forgiveness to every close bond. You tend to attract sensitive, creative or spiritually minded people, and your relationships often carry a sense of shared meaning that goes beyond the everyday. You are generous in love, quick to see the best in others and slow to condemn. That generosity can blur into overlooking what needs to be addressed, excusing behaviour that deserves a firmer response. When your idealism is matched by clear sight, your partnerships feel deeply connected and quietly inspired.",
    tension: "Your longing for an ideal love and the realities of partnership often clash. You fall for a vision of someone, then struggle when the real person steps out of the dream. Boundaries can blur, and you may give too much, lose yourself in a partner's needs, or attract people who are evasive, unreliable or dishonest. Confusion about what you want in a relationship is common, and you can feel let down more often than you admit. Sometimes you are the elusive one, hard to pin down and quietly slipping away when things become too real. This friction slowly teaches you discernment. When compassion is joined by clear boundaries, you find a love that is both real and beautiful."
  },
  "pluto|dsc": {
    theme: "Partnership is intense and transformative for you. Your deepest changes come through the people you bond with, and you seek relationships with real depth.",
    fusion: "Your relationships run deep and change you profoundly. You are drawn to intense, magnetic, powerful people, and the connections you form are rarely casual. Partnership is where you meet your own depths: desire, jealousy, loyalty and the fear of loss. You are fiercely committed once you trust someone, and you want complete honesty in return. The difficulty lies in power: control, possessiveness or manipulation can creep in from either side, and you may attract partners who dominate or whom you try to dominate. As you learn to share power rather than fight over it, your relationships become places of genuine rebirth.",
    flow: "Depth comes naturally to your relationships. You form bonds that are loyal, honest and emotionally rich, and partners feel truly seen by you, often more deeply than they have been seen before. You have a gift for helping the people you love through crises, and relationships often transform both of you in positive ways. You attract strong, perceptive people, and close business alliances can be powerful. The ease can make you comfortable with an intensity that others find overwhelming, so lighter partners may feel out of their depth. When your depth is matched by playfulness and trust, your partnerships become a source of lasting strength.",
    tension: "Your need for control and the surrender that partnership asks for are locked in a struggle. You want complete intimacy, yet you fear being vulnerable to another person's power. Relationships can become battlegrounds of jealousy, possessiveness or hidden agendas, and you may attract partners who try to control you or become controlling yourself. Endings can be dramatic, and each one leaves you changed. Trust comes slowly after past betrayals, and you test people long before you let them close. This friction is intense, but it forces a deep reckoning with how you handle power and intimacy. When the need to control loosens, you find relationships that are profoundly healing."
  },
  "chiron|dsc": {
    theme: "Partnership touches your deepest wound, and it is also where healing happens. You are drawn to people who mirror your hurts and help you mend them.",
    fusion: "Relationships touch the tenderest part of you. You carry an old sense of being unworthy of love or somehow different in partnership, and you often attract people who carry wounds of their own. You are a natural healer in relationships, offering compassion and understanding that others rarely find. The difficulty is repeating painful patterns: feeling rejected, choosing partners who need fixing, or putting up with too little. Intimacy can feel frightening because it brings the wound to the surface. As you tend your own hurt, your relationships become places where both people are healed, and your empathy deepens into real wisdom.",
    flow: "Partnership is a place where healing comes naturally for you. You understand pain from the inside, and you offer partners compassion without judgement. Relationships tend to help you work through old hurts gently, and you attract people who recognise your sensitivity and value it rather than exploit it. You are a gifted counsellor or mentor in one to one settings, because others feel safe opening up to you. The ease can make you the helper in every relationship, rarely the one being helped, and your own needs slip quietly into the background. When care flows both ways, your bonds become truly restorative.",
    tension: "Your old wounds and your relationships keep meeting. Just when you feel close, an old hurt surfaces, and you pull away, overcompensate or feel rejected all over again. You may attract partners who reopen the same wound, or become the one who tries to fix people who do not want fixing. Feeling not good enough in love is a familiar ache, and you can hide it behind competence or independence. This friction is painful, but it brings the wound into the open where it can finally heal. Over time you develop remarkable compassion, and your relationships become a place of genuine repair, for you and for the people you love."
  },
  "northNode|dsc": {
    theme: "Your growth lies in partnership. You are learning to share, cooperate and let others in, and your path opens through close relationships.",
    fusion: "Your direction in life runs through other people. You are learning to cooperate, compromise and share your life rather than go it alone, and the most meaningful turning points often arrive through partners. Instinctively you lean toward independence and self reliance, yet relationships keep drawing you out of that habit. You are drawn to people who bring qualities you are meant to develop in yourself. The difficulty is resisting that pull, clinging to self sufficiency or feeling threatened by needing someone. As you open to partnership, you discover a fuller version of yourself, and your relationships become the path to your purpose.",
    flow: "Partnership supports your growth with a quiet ease. The right people tend to appear when you need them, and relationships help you move toward your purpose rather than away from it. Cooperation comes more naturally than you once expected, and you learn a great deal from the people you commit to. Close alliances in business and love tend to open doors and point you in a meaningful direction. The ease can make you passive, waiting for others to lead the way or define the path for you. When you bring your full self to your partnerships, they become a steady road toward meaning.",
    tension: "Your drive for independence and your need for partnership sit in real tension. You feel the pull to go it alone, yet life keeps bringing you into situations that demand cooperation and compromise. Balancing your own needs with a partner's can feel like a constant negotiation, and you swing between putting yourself first and losing yourself entirely. Relationships at key moments seem to test your sense of direction, forcing choices between the familiar path and the one that asks more of you. This friction clarifies what kind of partnership truly supports your growth. When you find it, your relationships and your purpose begin to move together."
  },
  "lilith|dsc": {
    theme: "Partnership stirs your untamed, unapologetic side. You are drawn to intense, unconventional people, and you refuse to shrink yourself to fit a relationship.",
    fusion: "Relationships bring out your wildest and most unapologetic side. You are drawn to magnetic, rebellious or forbidden partners, and you often meet your own suppressed desire and anger through them. You refuse to be tamed in love, and you rarely accept a relationship that asks you to be smaller than you are. Power, sexuality and control are strong themes in your partnerships. The difficulty is intensity: jealousy, rejection or feeling exiled within a relationship can wound deeply, and you may attract people who are volatile or dismissive. As you claim your own desire without shame, your partnerships become places of honesty, equality and real freedom.",
    flow: "Your independent spirit sits comfortably within partnership. You attract people who respect your strength, and you bring passion, honesty and a refusal to play games to your relationships. You are at ease with desire and with difference, and you give partners room to be themselves in turn. Unconventional arrangements suit you, and you have little interest in what a relationship is supposed to look like. The ease can make you dismissive of vulnerability, or of partners who want more tenderness than you readily offer. When your fierceness is paired with openness, your relationships feel alive, honest and free of pretence.",
    tension: "Your need for freedom and your desire for a partner collide sharply. You refuse to be controlled in love, yet you may attract relationships where control is exactly the issue, or feel rejected for being too much. Hidden desire, resentment and power struggles can simmer beneath the surface of your bonds. Part of you wants to be fully accepted, while another part expects to be pushed away. You swing between rebellion and compliance, sometimes within the same relationship. This friction forces you to own your desire and your anger instead of projecting them onto a partner. Once you do, you find relationships where your full self is welcome."
  },
  "fortune|dsc": {
    theme: "Your happiness is closely linked to partnership. Joy, ease and good luck tend to come through the people you commit to.",
    fusion: "Much of your happiness arrives through partnership. You flourish when you share your life with someone, and good fortune often comes through a partner, whether as love, opportunity or practical support. You bring warmth and an easy sense of joy to relationships, and people enjoy being close to you. Business alliances can prove lucky as well, since others want to succeed alongside you. The difficulty is depending on a partner for your contentment, or feeling lost and flat without one. As you find joy within yourself as well as through others, your relationships become a source of genuine and lasting happiness rather than the only place it lives.",
    flow: "Contentment flows naturally through your relationships. You tend to meet the right people at the right time, and partnerships bring you comfort, pleasure and practical good luck. You know how to create harmony with another person, and shared ventures often prosper. People sense that being with you makes life easier and brighter, and they return that feeling generously. The ease can make you take a good relationship for granted, assuming the goodwill will always be there without tending it. When you invest as much as you receive, your partnerships become one of the deepest sources of well being in your life.",
    tension: "Your personal happiness and your partnerships do not always point the same way. What makes you content alone can clash with what a relationship asks of you, and you may feel you have to choose between your own joy and a partner's. You can look to relationships for a happiness that keeps slipping away, or feel that luck arrives only when you are single. Adjusting your expectations takes real effort, and disappointment can linger when a bond fails to deliver what you hoped. This friction teaches you where contentment truly lies. Once you know, both your own life and your partnerships feel lighter and more rewarding."
  },
  "vertex|dsc": {
    theme: "Fated meetings shape your relationships. The partners who matter most often arrive through circumstances that feel destined, and they change the direction of your life.",
    fusion: "Destiny seems to play a hand in your relationships. Significant partners often arrive through chance encounters or circumstances beyond your control, and these meetings tend to alter the course of your life. You feel a strong sense of recognition with certain people, as though you were meant to find each other. Relationships carry a karmic quality, bringing lessons you could not have learned alone. The difficulty is surrendering to these encounters without losing your own agency, or waiting for fate when a choice is yours to make. As you accept the meaningful timing of your partnerships, you find that the people you meet are exactly the ones you need.",
    flow: "Meaningful people arrive in your life with a quiet ease. You tend to meet partners and allies at the right moment, often through circumstances that feel gently arranged. These relationships support your growth and open doors that stay closed to you on your own. You recognise a significant connection quickly and are willing to follow where it leads, trusting your sense that something important has begun. The ease can make you passive, waiting for fate to deliver rather than taking part in shaping the bond. When you meet these encounters with openness and commitment, they shape a rich and purposeful life.",
    tension: "Fated encounters and your own plans often collide. Significant people tend to arrive at inconvenient moments, disrupting your life and forcing choices you did not expect to face. You may feel pulled toward relationships that challenge your independence or your sense of control, and resisting them only seems to make them more insistent. Some of these meetings bring difficult lessons, and you can fight them at first. Part of you wants to decide everything for yourself, while life keeps placing the key to your growth in someone else's hands. This friction ultimately reveals what you most need from partnership. When you stop fighting the timing, these encounters become turning points that lead somewhere meaningful."
  }
});
